        "content": "<p>I'm wondering if someone might have a suggestion for formalizing the definition of a Kripke model for intuitionistic propositional logic as described <a href=\"https://cs.uwaterloo.ca/~plragde/flaneries/LACI/Propositional_Logic.html#%28part._.Kripke%29\">here</a>:<br>\n\"A Kripke model is a tree and a relation (sometimes called the \"forcing relation\") between nodes of the tree and propositional variables.\"<br>\nI would like to be able to use it in exercise 7 further below. Does something like the following make the most sense here, or is there something more abstract that might be a better choice?</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Data</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Defs</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">inductive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Model</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">node</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">xs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Model</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
